{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/812309-balance-of-magic-and-technology-help","id":812309,"title":"balance of magic and technology help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-19T19:36:04-08:00","id":812309,"title":"balance of magic and technology help","content":"Hi I\u2019m working on a campaign for my group of gamers. I\u2019m having a hard time trying to keep a balance of magic and technology in my game. Do you have any tips for that and for what to do with human and non human bodies?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11063-dalurain","name":"dalurain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T20:17:10-08:00","id":812342,"title":"","content":"You may want to provide more details as to what exactly you want. What do you mean you're trying to keep a balance between magic and tech? What kind of balance? And what do you mean what to do with human and non human bodies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T20:47:29-08:00","id":812356,"title":"","content":"Well im trying to figure out how far I can push both magic and tech before it becomes easy for humans to see the magic or tech to over power the supernatural. What I mean by the bodies is what are some good ideas about how the players can get rid of the bodies of humans and creatures after killing them. i may still not sound clear to you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11063-dalurain","name":"dalurain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T21:52:05-08:00","id":812386,"title":"","content":"No, I get what you're saying now. One of the stated problems with detecting supernaturals isn't that they're necessarily hard to spot, per se. In general, 2e seems to assume that people, at least on a subconscious level are <i>aware</i> that there are things that go bump in the night, but they're psychologically inclined to <i>ignore that</i>. So while an increase in tech may make them easier to detect, people would still have to deal with that inclination to try to reason what they're seeing away as something mundane, or forget it altogether. Though there are some forces, like Quiescence, Lunacy, Spoofing, and Changelings Masks that actively impede a persons ability to perceive something nature regardless of what sort of method they use, some of which are more airtight than others.<br /> <br /> As for at what point tech starts to overpower supernatural abilities...I guess once you get to the tech levels that seem to work like magic. Once you start getting into the kind of technology that modern day people would see as magic, then you'd probably be getting into the realm of technology outdoing actual magic. Maybe. It depends on the specifics to be honest.<br /> <br /> Now hiding bodies is something that also varies significantly depending on the supernatural in question. Depending on the method of murder, one of the supernaturals might not <i>need</i> to hide the body since it would be highly unlikely that given the cause of death a human(ish) source would be suspected. If a werewolf or mage killed someone by summoning a bolt of lightning to strike them down it would just seem like a freak accident. Mind controlling a person into killing themselves can easily be played off as a normal suicide. In general, I feel it's easier to kill people in ways that mundane authorities simply can't track is easier to get away with than slicing someone to bits and trying to hide the body.<br /> <br /> Though if you <i>really</i> need to dump a body somewhere and you have the means to, tossing the corpses of your victims in the Shadow or other strange planes of existence works fairly well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T03:05:25-08:00","id":812474,"title":"","content":"Let's see... A vampire with obfuscate could stroll down a crowded street with a corpse without anyone noticing, werewolves have a Nature facet that gets rid of corpses, or they could dump it in the shadow, or they could just eat it, Mages can either annihilate it with fire, or turn it into a chair, or dump it in the shadow, Changeling can dump things in the hedge, Beasts can dump shit in their Lair, sin eaters might get away with dumping a body in the underworld (but that seems a little tactless), Demons are all <i>about</i> not getting caught, prometheans... can't really be held in a cell for too long before the door falls off, and everyone has means of killing people that wouldn't look like a murder. <br /> <br /> I mean, pretty much every splat can turn into an animal in one way or another, for starters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T04:26:49-08:00","id":812489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dalurain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/812309-balance-of-magic-and-technology-help?p=812356#post812356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well im trying to figure out how far I can push both magic and tech before it becomes easy for humans to see the magic or tech to over power the supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div> Like Ashenrogue said, its not that technology can't detect the supernatural - it can. There's actually evidence out there. But humanity is more inclined to ignore that evidence than it is to embrace it. In some cases (the God-Machine, Mage and its Quintessence, the Kiss, Lunacy), its an actual supernatural compulsion to force people to ignore what's going on around them. They literally can't acknowledge the supernatural exists. When humans start acknowledging the supernatural, that's when hunters are born.<br /> <br /> As for technology &quot;overpowering&quot; the supernatural... I don't think it does. Magic and technology work side by side - they're not mutually opposed to each other. In many cases, the technology has magical components to it that can be manipulated. Werewolves flat out ask the animistic spirit of technological devices to do things for the wolf. There's no overpowering that, because that'd be like saying the device is overpowering itself, which is kind of silly. <br /> <br /> Some supernaturals have powers that make technology ignore them. And that's because these supernaturals are bending the laws of physics that the technology relies on to work. You can't overpower that without realizing that's entirely possible to bend the laws of physics in the first place!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I mean by the bodies is what are some good ideas about how the players can get rid of the bodies of humans and creatures after killing them. i may still not sound clear to you. </div> </div> </div> Depends on a lot of things. With werewolves, you have to be careful if there's bite marks, and where to dispose of the body so you don't start piling up negative spirits. Werewolves have a tendacy to create a lot of anger, pain, and death spirits with their job balancing their territories. So that's a concern as well. I like using deserts or oceans, myself. They're so large, that you can go anywhere to hide a body, and the spirits would fall to slumber in time due to starvation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T08:42:13-08:00","id":812636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/812309-balance-of-magic-and-technology-help?p=812489#post812489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves flat out ask the animistic spirit of technological devices to do things for the wolf. There's no overpowering that, because that'd be like saying the device is overpowering itself, which is kind of silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, unless the technology employs some mechanism to prevent its own spirit from obeying external commands. What technology might that be? I don't know (but the God-Machine probably does).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/812309-balance-of-magic-and-technology-help?p=812489#post812489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some supernaturals have powers that make technology ignore them. And that's because these supernaturals are bending the laws of physics that the technology relies on to work. You can't overpower that without realizing that's entirely possible to bend the laws of physics in the first place!</div> </div> </div> </div>You just need to interfere with their interfering with physics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/812309-balance-of-magic-and-technology-help?p=812489#post812489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on a lot of things. With werewolves, you have to be careful if there's bite marks, and where to dispose of the body so you don't start piling up negative spirits. Werewolves have a tendacy to create a lot of anger, pain, and death spirits with their job balancing their territories. So that's a concern as well. I like using deserts or oceans, myself. They're so large, that you can go anywhere to hide a body, and the spirits would fall to slumber in time due to starvation.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is were a &quot;garbage disposal&quot; magath would come in handy. Generate unwanted spirits? Feed them to the Omnimatic! What could possibly go wrong?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T08:53:52-08:00","id":812647,"title":"","content":"&quot;Oh, so <i>that's </i>where idigam come from...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T10:39:43-08:00","id":812711,"title":"","content":"There's a piece of fiction in Danse Macabre where a vampire, Earth, visits some of his werewolf friends to see if they can help him dispose of a body. They didn't take it well, though it was in first edition and the taboo was stronger there. I could easily imagine a Bale Hound of Gluttony allowing services like that, similar to the cleaner from John Wick. Someone you can call up and make someone disappear, though perhaps being unaware that they're stealing secrets from the corpse and compiling all the evidence they could possibly want to control you.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you don't like the taste, and even my werewolf would balk at the idea of eating someone's leftovers, werewolves do have a way to access an entire other world where they can just drop bodies. I always liked this idea because it seems like it could lead to so much fun for the storyteller, with spirit scavengers enjoying the taste of Essence.<br /> <br /> Then there's the obvious ways. Gifts. Moldywarp allows you to dig holes really fast, Black Earth, Red Hunger actually disposes of bodies very well, and there's a few things you could do with the Gifts of the Elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}